  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mental Health, Behaviour Change and Social Inclusion Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Mental Health, Behaviour Change and Social Inclusion Project is a two year project run by the Fatima Institute of the Diocese of Makeni which will promote mental health, behaviour change, social inclusion and sustainable livelihoods with the overall aim of strengthening peace and security in Sierra Leone. Project partners will identify those in need of assistance, develop a curriculum and teach government and non-government stakeholders to respond appropriately to mental health needs, educate the broader public via radio, facilitate rehabilitated clients&apos; entry into livelihoods programmes and/or refer them for further assistance.</narrative>
  </description>
